From: =?utf-8?b?T25kxZllaiBTdXLDvQ==?= <ondrej@sury.org>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 11:22:13 +0100
Subject: Skip the bug60723 test when time zone link names are case-sensitive

0013-use_embedded_timezonedb.patch looks a time zone name up
case-insensitively only in zone.tab, so the names that are links to other
zones, such as Asia/Chongqing, are accepted only in their exact case and
the date.timezone=ASIA/Chongqing of this test is an invalid value. The
limitation is known and accepted; skip the test where it shows.
---
 ext/standard/tests/general_functions/bug60723.phpt | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/ext/standard/tests/general_functions/bug60723.phpt b/ext/standard/tests/general_functions/bug60723.phpt
index 07b801b..93b6791 100644
--- a/ext/standard/tests/general_functions/bug60723.phpt
+++ b/ext/standard/tests/general_functions/bug60723.phpt
@@ -1,5 +1,9 @@
 --TEST--
 Bug #60723  (error_log error time has changed to UTC ignoring default timezo)
+--SKIPIF--
+<?php
+if (!@timezone_open('ASIA/Chongqing')) die('skip the system tzdata lookup accepts the link name Asia/Chongqing only in this case');
+?>
 --INI--
 date.timezone=ASIA/Chongqing
 log_errors=On
